  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that (E)-Cinnamyl (E)-Cinnamate may interact with SMMC-7721 through multiple pathways, with the target SMMC-7721 being influenced by several intermediates. Specifically, (E)-Cinnamyl (E)-Cinnamate is linked to Caspase-5, which is targeted by 2,4-Bis[(4-hydroxyphenyl)methyl]-5-methoxy-3-[2-(3-methoxyphenyl)ethyl]phenol, and further to SMMC-7721. Similarly, (E)-Cinnamyl (E)-Cinnamate is also associated with Microtubule-associated protein 1B, which is targeted by 6-Hydroxy-2-[2-(2-hydroxyphenyl) ethyl]chromone, which also targets SMMC-7721. These findings indicate that (E)-Cinnamyl (E)-Cinnamate may exert its biological effects through distinct molecular mechanisms, potentially modulating cellular processes that influence SMMC-7721's behavior. The evidence is consistent with the possibility that (E)-Cinnamyl (E)-Cinnamate acts as a modulator of signaling pathways that ultimately affect SMMC-7721, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
